> ## aw. Named actions (motion/REPORT.md, inventory/REPORT.md)
> - 300 blind packs (176 actions, 124 assets), two blind passes (A on full+crop sheets, B adds difference sheets), a third pass on 34 disputed actions. Consensus (two of three within 2 f): 164 of 176. Caveat: labellers repeatedly lost images from context; several items were labelled from notes or memory (listed in the report); the third labeller's first 16 items were labelled from memory.
> - Timing per named action (consensus items; frames, ms = f x 33.3; window cap 48 f): lift 6 f (200 ms), turn 4.5 (150), react 5 (167), point 5 (167), stand 7.25 (242), talk 7.5 (250), emote 7 (233), fall 10.5 (350, ease-in), throw 8 (267, anticipation in all labels), pull 9 (300), recoil 9.75 (325, snap), sit 6.5, drop 13.5 (ease-in), push 13.5, catch 3.25, walk 14 (linear, capped). Most are ease-out; all read as 2D cutout (rigid card parts) with squash and stretch rare. n is 3 to 12 per action: small-n guidance.
> - Missing actions: recipes by analogy in `motion/INFERRED_RECIPES.md` (sneak, run, stumble, carry, catch, wave, push, drop). The inference test says durations and limbs are about 70 % right and easing is a guess.
> 
> ## ax. Body mechanics and asset physics
> - Measurable: arm curvature (89.1 % pair agreement), no squash and stretch in most actions, anticipation only for throws, overshoot rare, feet move in walk/stand/fall. Not measurable from strips: joint angles, stride length, cadence, loop length, hair and clothing motion (clothing 46 %). Earlier cadence (7.5 f per step, uncertain) stands.
> - Assets: durations by behaviour (frames median): drifts 28.5, particle bursts 14.25, falls 12.5 (ease-in 13 of 20), rotates 9.5, slides 19.25, flows 29, loops 38, sways 25 (ease-in-out). Bounces are rare (9 items, 7 in one video). Gravity reference stays 4.7 to 5.1 screen heights per s^2 (loop 3 tools). Inferred recipes for cloth, animals, crowds in the same file.
> 
> ## ay. Camera and layers, second attempt (camera/REPORT.md)
> - Harder known-answer set (64 moves, 100 to 300 f, whip pans, cuts, moving characters): S1 and S2 failed most marks (S2 tilt 95.3 % passes); whip pans broke both solvers; the character plane was only 6 to 11 % of the frame. On 192 real moves the solvers agree scale 53.1, roll 43.2, pan 27.1, tilt 27.6, layer ranking 12.0; focal length self-calibration worked on synthetic clips (8 of 8) but found no usable segment in Rick's videos, which may mean his camera is not a single pinhole camera (untested reading). Parallax and layer shifts remain unmeasured. Use the loop-2 screen-space numbers and the v1.4/v1.5 duration recipes; scale ratios stay soft (push-in about 1.3 to 1.4, pull-out about 0.6 to 0.8).
> - Nothing stays locked on screen inside a Rick shot (median locked share 0, indicative).
